    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d160">

                <pb facs="0381" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v01/pg359"/>

                <head>160. Memorandum of a Telephone Conversation Between the Secretary of State and
                    the Director of the Bureau of the Budget (Bell)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d160-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1961-10-12T14:57:00-04:00"
                                >October 12, 1961, 2:57 p.m.</date></hi></dateline></opener>
                <p>The Sec said Viet-Nam can be critical and we would like to throw in resources
                    rather than people if we can. Can we in the Depts involved if the Pres directs
                    it be done put the costs on it on a chit and go to Congress in early January for
                    the necessary special action? B said no problem at all with respect to Defense.
                    They have special authority for military aid. CIA no problem. Contingency fund exists for State and economic aid
                    so that should mean this is all right. If the Sec wants a more precise answer B
                    should put Hansen<anchor n="2" xml:id="d160-f2"/> in touch with whoever is
                    working on it and it should be worked out before they go too far down the
                    road.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
